(FIL-03, FIL-04: readable is true iff open for reading, writable iff
 open for writing - appending counts as writing for this property, hand-
 verified. LANGUAGE.md:3808-3809. A file is seeded first (writing mode
 always succeeds, even on a path that does not exist yet), then reopened
 in a DRAWN mode - reading, writing or appending - so which mode a given
 program tests varies across the corpus. Probe:
 docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-04.vox.)

