(FIL-05, FIL-06: modified and accessed return Unix timestamps -
 LANGUAGE.md:3810-3811. Bounded on both sides: never below 1 (never 0 or
 negative), and never after `current time's unix` - the manual gives a
 clock (LANGUAGE.md:4564, the `unix` time property), so "not in the future" is assertable
 exactly rather than as a wide fixed floor. Prints a fixed marker on
 success, never the raw timestamp - see 'gen file assert range
 quietly's own comment for why. Probe: docs/ledger/probes/files/
 FIL-06.vox.)

